    "updated_at": "2024-09-23T18:28:44Z",
    "body": "Sorry, here's a native contrived(?) example replacing what React is sort of doing: https://jsbin.com/zipeket/edit?html,css,js,output.\r\n\r\nNote that if I used `<slot>`'s here and just flipped the Slot's `name` attribute I wouldn't be replacing DOM elements and by that maintain state.\r\nHowever, JS frameworks recreate elements from templates, as in the example above, and by that we lose state.\r\n\r\nTo see the effect click \"Tab 2\" > click the \"This is Pane 2\" text > it changes color > click \"Tab 1\" > click \"Tab 2\" > state is lost.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
