    "updated_at": "2024-09-24T00:21:45Z",
    "body": "> I'm not sure we'd want to add this to CustomStateSet, since CustomStateSet is meant to emulate the behavior of native elements / pseudo-classes, and native elements have the same behavior\r\n\r\nTrue, but that is how they already behave OOTB.\r\nI'm suggesting an enhancement on top of existing default behavior. Perhaps we could extend this to native form elements as well?\r\n\r\nWe need to consider here that the developer controlling the host and the one controlling the custom element are not necessarily the same one.\r\nI actually had this use-case, but then realized this will only solve half of my problems, and I'll still have to maintain that state externally some how.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
